<title>USA: Staffmark Inc Q4 shr $0.20.</title>
<headline>Staffmark Inc Q4 shr $0.20.</headline>
<dateline>FAYETTEVILLE, Ark. 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>		    Quarters Ended Dec. 31,  Years Ended Dec. 31,</p>
<p>					1996    1995	1996     1995</p>
<p>				 (unaudited)  (unaudited) (unaudited)</p>
<p> Service revenues	    $55,901 $40,472  $198,444 $146,687</p>
<p> Cost of services	     43,344  32,175   155,472  117,103</p>
<p>   Gross profit		 12,557   8,297    42,972   29,584</p>
<p>Operating expenses:</p>
<p>Selling, General</p>
<p>    and administrative	 7,971   7,297    29,840   24,069</p>
<p>Depreciation and</p>
<p>    amortization		   509     393     1,911    1,157</p>
<p>   Operating income	    4,077     607    11,221    4,358</p>
<p>		    Quarters Ended Dec. 31,  Years Ended Dec. 31,</p>
<p>				   1996     1995	  1996     1995</p>
<p>					   Pro Forma (1)  Pro Forma(1)</p>
<p> Net income		   $2,597    $297	$6,368   $3,106</p>
<p>Net income per common share</p>
<p>				    0.20    0.04	  0.67     0.37</p>
<p>Weighted average</p>
<p>  shares outstanding	13,242   8,300	 9,545    8,300</p>
<p>(1)  Pro forma net income and EPS are unaudited and reflect the financial results of the companies which merged effective with the IPO as if the companies had been members of the same operating group adjusted to reflect the effect of acquisitions, corporate income taxes and reduction in owners compensation.</p>
<p>(2)  Operating results for 1996 will be reported in accordance with the provisions of SEC staff Accounting Bulletin No. 97.  </p>
<p>This pronouncement requires that one of the original Founding Companies be identified as the acquirer for financial reporting purposes.</p>
<p>Therefore, results reported for the periods prior to the IPO will represent only the operations of the identified acquiring company rather than the combined operating results as shown above.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
